+# Password Hashing Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Argon2id as the password hashing algorithm. It was chosen for its resistance to GPU-accelerated brute-force attacks (through its memory-hard design) and to side-channel timing attacks, which makes it the current best practice for password storage in new systems. No specific parameter values (memory cost, iterations, parallelism) are recorded, so none are set by this policy.
